Original commit body from f4c6644f4091954bdfaa285b70dcde0a536e339d:

Rewires the release pipeline for the post-cutover GitHub backend so a tagged
release builds + publishes on GitHub instead of the retired self-hosted
Forgejo/Codeberg path. Lands dormant — it only fires once GitHub Actions is
enabled and a v* tag is pushed (Phase 4 human steps). Ref:
migration-phase2-5-design.md Part 3.6.

- release.yml: every `runs-on: self-hosted` -> `ubuntu-latest`; the
  "Create Forgejo Release" step becomes `gh release create` (Actions-injected
  GITHUB_TOKEN + `permissions: contents: write`); drop the Codeberg
  nightly-status pre-check job and the self-hosted post-publish
  matrix/integration jobs (multi-Python + integration now run on the
  Woodpecker `nightly` cron); keep build/checksums/SBOM/twine->PyPI.
  FORGEJO_TOKEN reaches zero refs. Delete the obsolete release-mirror.yml
  (it mirrored a release *from* Codeberg — nothing to mirror from now).
- prepare-release: Step 7 (dev->main PR) is backend-aware. The Codeberg AGit
  `refs/for/main` push stays byte-identical (both push-option guard tests
  preserved); the GitHub backend creates the PR from the already-pushed `dev`
  via the approved forge lib (`create_pr dev main`), never a raw API call,
  with an honest manual fallback. Handoff strings de-Codeberg'd.
- tag-release: advisory URLs are backend-aware (the tag push already targets
  origin=GitHub; only the human-facing links were stale).
- RELEASE_SOP.md: pipeline-topology + secrets table updated to the two-job
  GitHub-Actions workflow.
- Add a guard test locking the GitHub Step-7 `create_pr` path.

